4. The matter is admittedly governed by the provisions of Rajasthan Civil Services (New Pay Scales) Rules 1969 read with Education Subordinate Service Rules, 1971. It may, however, be stated that the scales have been revised subsequently. The amount of Rs. 130/- per month was fixed as the salary of the respondent in accordance with the provisions in the Schedule which reads as follows;
Freshly recruited untrained graduates in this scale will receive fixed pay of Rs. 130/-until he gets trained.
The above provision has been struck down by the High Court in part on the ground of illegal discrimination and the appellant has been directed to pay the respondent his salary at the higher rate for the period 1972 to 1982 also during which period he was an untrained teacher. This view has been challenged on behalf of the appellant as untenable.

